    {
      name = [[Dungeons]],
      sections = {
        {
          title = [[Why dungeons (Forever)]],
          short = [[Why]],
          icon = [[INV_Misc_Key_03]],
          lines = {
            [[- Take every quest for a dungeon |cff7fd35bbefore|r you go in. Kill XP inside is small; quest XP is big.]],
            [[- The final boss of a 15-25 dungeon counts towards a Legacy point (World tab).]],
          },
        },
        {
          title = [[Your first dungeon, step by step]],
          short = [[How to]],
          icon = [[INV_Misc_Book_09]],
          lines = {
            [[- |cffffd1001. Pick up the quests|r first (Now tab lists them). Quest XP is the big reward.]],
            [[- |cffffd1002. Find a group|r (Groups section). Say you're a bear tank and new: most groups are happy to explain.]],
            [[- |cffffd1003. Walk to the entrance|r: there are no summoning stones or teleports in Forever, so everyone travels there. Deadmines: the mine in Moonbrook|cff9d9d9d (about 42, 72)|r; inside, follow the tunnel down to the swirling portal.]],
            [[- |cffffd1004. Before each pull|r: wait for the healer's mana, say the target in /p ("skull first"), then pull with Moonfire or Faerie Fire and back round a corner.]],
            [[- |cffffd1005. Fight|r: Swipe for packs, Maul the skull, Growl anything that runs to the healer. Don't chase runners: they bring friends.]],
            [[- |cffffd1006. Loot|r: the Loot roll advice box marks the button to press (it checks your gear, the price and who else in the party wears it). Most quest items can be looted by everyone who has the quest: check before you leave a boss.]],
            [[- |cffffd1007. If you wipe|r: release, run back as a ghost to the entrance, and rejoin. Ask the group to wait for you.]],
            [[- |cffffd1008. After the last boss|r: loot quest items, then hand in back in town (Now tab: Hand in, in order).]],
          },
        },
        {
          title = [[Finding a group (no automatic finder)]],
          short = [[Groups]],
          icon = [[Spell_Holy_PrayerOfHealing]],
          lines = {
            [[- |cffffd1001. List yourself|r: green-eye button, Looking for Group. Pick The Deadmines, tick Tank and Damage, note "druid, new, have quests", press List. Keep questing; accept the invite pop-up.]],
            [[- |cffffd1002. Browse|r: same window. Find a group missing your role and whisper the leader: "hi, druid, tank or DPS, have the quests".]],
            [[- |cffffd1003. Chat|r: /1 LFG Deadmines, druid tank/DPS (in Westfall or Stormwind).]],
            [[- Then everyone walks to the entrance: no summoning stones. Say you're new; ask the group to wait while you get any quests they share.]],
            [[- It usually takes 10-20 minutes. Quest while you wait.]],
            [[- |cffffd100Rolls|r: the Loot roll advice box marks the button to press, and checks your party so you stay polite.]],
            [[|cff9d9d9dSources: kami-labs (Forever client data), Warcraft Tavern, Icy Veins.|r]],
          },
        },
        {
          title = [[Rolling on loot (be nice)]],
          short = [[Rolls]],
          icon = [[INV_Misc_Coin_01]],
          lines = {
            [[- The |cffffd100Loot roll advice|r box pops up with each roll and marks the button to press, e.g. >Greed<. You still click.]],
            [[- |cffffd100NEED|r: a real upgrade for you. Cloth? It tells you to ask first: cloth is for mages, priests and warlocks.]],
            [[- |cffffd100GREED|r: small upgrades someone else wants more, off-role pieces, items for a few levels from now, recipes and materials.]],
            [[- |cffffd100Never Need|r just to sell something. That gets people kicked.]],
            [[- Druids wear cloth and leather only (never mail or plate, no shields). Weapons: staves, daggers, maces, fist weapons.]],
            [[- Gear you'll grow into (up to 5 levels) is kept in your bags, never sold.]],
            [[- If the leader sets loot rules ("Need main role only"), follow them over the box.]],
            [[- Won something someone else needed? A "sorry, gz" in /p goes a long way.]],
          },
        },
